    "content": "The inaugural Java House Grand Prix of Arlington took place from March 13–15, 2026, featuring an IndyCar street race around AT&T Stadium and Globe Life Field. Kyle Kirkwood won the race on Sunday, March 15, taking the INDYCAR series lead. The 2.73-mile track featured 14 turns and brought IndyCar, Indy NXT, and supporting racing to the North Texas area. Event Details Race Winner: Kyle Kirkwood (AJ Foyt Racing). Track Location: Arlington Entertainment District (Surrounding AT&T Stadium & Globe Life Field). Circuit Length: 2.73 miles. Date: March 13-15, 2026. Key Takeaways Inaugural Race: The event marked the first-ever IndyCar race in Arlington. Winning Performance: Kyle Kirkwood outdueled Alex Palou in the final laps to win. Other Races: Max Taylor won the INDY NXT event. Weather Impact: Sunday concerts were canceled due to high winds. About the CircuitThe track is designed to showcase the Arlington Entertainment District, with spectator areas near major venues, including Choctaw Stadium. The 2026 weekend included practice, qualifying, and the main race, with broadcasting on FOX.",
